1
00:00:01,130 --> 00:00:06,950
Learn meaning of words.

2
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:13,510
woodcutter

3
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:18,060
Buddha

4
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,110
wood

5
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:29,000
axe blade

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:37,640
gray hair

7
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:50,060
Observe pictures to understand words.

8
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:59,040
Woodcutter: is person who cuts wood for living.

9
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:15,480
Buddha: is kind person with magic, often helps kind, unlucky people (imaginary character).

10
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:23,260
Read paragraph one again.

11
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:34,350
Long ago, there was a kind, diligent young woodcutter, every day went to forest to chop wood to earn living.

12
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:42,130
One day, he swung axe to chop a dry tree, axe blade flew into river.

13
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:47,260
River deep, water fast, hard to dive in.

14
00:01:47,260 --> 00:02:00,110
What bad luck happened to woodcutter?

15
00:02:00,110 --> 00:02:05,770
Ah, woodcutter's axe blade flew into river.

16
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:14,170
River deep, water fast, hard to retrieve axe.

17
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:24,800
Read paragraph two again.

18
00:02:37,350 --> 00:02:44,620
Suddenly, an old gray-haired old man appeared

19
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:52,530
Hearing woodcutter's story old man said: - I can retrieve axe for you.

20
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:56,370
As soon as finished, old man jumped into river.

21
00:02:56,370 --> 00:03:03,330
In a blink, he raised a shining golden axe blade.

22
00:03:03,330 --> 00:03:06,480
Is this your axe? - Old man asked.

23
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:13,530
Grandpa, this axe blade is not mine.

24
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:24,770
When axe fell into river, who did woodcutter meet?

25
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:36,040
An old gray-haired old man suddenly appeared, promised to retrieve axe for woodcutter.

26
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:45,420
Old man dove into river first time and retrieved what to give woodcutter?

27
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,860
Choose correct answer.

28
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:51,330
A. Iron axe blade.

29
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:55,600
B. Silver axe blade.

30
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:01,930
C. Golden axe blade.

31
00:04:04,730 --> 00:04:12,220
Answer: C. Golden axe blade.

32
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:26,910
Golden axe blade is very precious, very valuable. Did woodcutter accept? Why not?

33
00:04:26,910 --> 00:04:34,730
Woodcutter did not accept because it was not his axe blade.

34
00:04:35,770 --> 00:04:44,600
What happened next? Read paragraph three.

35
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:54,480
Old man again dove into river and raised a shining silver axe blade.

36
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:58,150
Surely this is your axe?

37
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:01,930
Grandpa, this axe blade is also not mine.

38
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:10,310
Dove into river second time, old man retrieved what to give woodcutter?

39
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:15,260
A. Iron axe blade.

40
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:20,040
B. Silver axe blade.

41
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:26,840
C. Golden axe blade.

42
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:37,860
Answer: B. Silver axe blade.

43
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:52,950
Silver axe blade is also precious, valuable. Did woodcutter accept? Why not?

44
00:05:54,640 --> 00:06:02,840
Woodcutter did not accept because it was not his axe blade.

45
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:14,420
What happened next? Read paragraph four.

46
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:32,060
Old man dove into river third time and retrieved what to give woodcutter?

47
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:36,750
Answer: A

48
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:44,350
Old man retrieved what to give woodcutter?

49
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:50,370
Did he accept?

50
00:06:50,370 --> 00:06:57,680
Third time, old man raised iron axe blade.

51
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:05,060
Woodcutter accepted and thanked old man.

52
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:17,600
How did story end? Continue reading paragraph four to know.

53
00:07:30,710 --> 00:07:44,480
Old man gave woodcutter both golden and silver axe blades.

